#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repository Style Guide"
msgstr "Panduan Gaya Repository"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "This page is a __work in progress__, and needs attention from experts on the subject, especially on fact checking."
msgstr "Halaman ini __masih dalam proses pengerjaan__, dan memerlukan perhatian dari para ahli di bidang ini, terutama untuk pemeriksaan fakta."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "This guide gives some more detailed information on what to store in metadata fields. Most items are outdated and will be merge with the manual over time."
msgstr "Panduan ini memberikan informasi lebih rinci mengenai nilai apa yang sebaiknya disimpan dalam bidang metadata. Sebagian besar informasinya sudah usang dan perlahan akan digabungkan ke dalam panduan utama."

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "*E.g* <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/tree/master>"
msgstr "*Contoh* <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/tree/master>"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "The F-Droid server does not directly publish an APK online, instead the F-Droid server needs a buildable source to build an APK from. This way the server guarantees that the resulting APK accurately represents the source code without any hidden anti-features."
msgstr "Server F-Droid tidak langsung memublikasikan APK secara online; server F-Droid memerlukan sumber yang dapat dibangun menjadi APK. Dengan cara ini, server memastikan bahwa APK yang dihasilkan sesuai dengan kode sumber asli tanpa adanya fitur tersembunyi yang tidak diinginkan."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Because F-Droid builds every app from its source code (via the Android SDK with ant, gradle or maven, sometimes with help from the Android NDK, standard GNU/Linux programs and a little pre-processing in the BASH shell), probably if you can see a file called _AndroidManifest.xml_ or _build.gradle_ in your sources then there are many possibilities that F-Droid will be able to build it."
msgstr "Karena F-Droid membangun setiap aplikasi dari source code-nya (melalui Android SDK dengan ant, gradle, atau maven, kadang dengan bantuan Android NDK, program GNU/Linux standar, dan sedikit pre-processing di shell BASH), kemungkinan besar jika Anda dapat melihat file bernama _AndroidManifest.xml_ atau _build.gradle_ di source Anda maka ada banyak kemungkinan F-Droid akan dapat membangunnya."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Note that most projects call upon pre-built libraries. The source code for these is found elsewhere. For ant, these will be found in the `libs/` folder and external ones are mentioned in the _project.properties_ files; for gradle, these will be mentioned in _build.gradle_ and are usually pulled from <http://mvnrepository.com>; for maven there will be `pom.xml` files which describe the dependencies.  If native code pre-built libraries are used, these will often be found in `res/raw/` or `assets/`: there should be something said about these in the _README_. The example above has one jar file dependency with a text reference and doesn't use any external libraries, so no extra references are needed."
msgstr "Perlu dicatat bahwa sebagian besar proyek memanggil library yang sudah dibangun sebelumnya. Source code untuk library tersebut berada di tempat lain. Untuk ant, library ini akan ditemukan di folder `libs/` dan yang eksternal disebutkan di file _project.properties_; untuk gradle, ini akan disebutkan di _build.gradle_ dan biasanya diambil dari <http://mvnrepository.com>; untuk maven akan ada file `pom.xml` yang menjelaskan dependensinya. Jika library pre-built native code digunakan, ini sering ditemukan di `res/raw/` atau `assets/`: harus ada penjelasan tentang ini di _README_. Contoh di atas memiliki satu dependensi file jar dengan referensi teks dan tidak menggunakan library eksternal apa pun, jadi tidak diperlukan referensi tambahan."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "- *E.g.* Overall: <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/blob/master/LICENSE> (overall of a source code under a *GPLv3+* license); - *E.g.* Source code header: <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/blob/master/app/src/main/java/org/fdroid/fdroid/AppDetails.java> (header of a file under a *GPLv3+* license); - *E.g.* Libraries: <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/tree/master/libs> (see the _LICENSE_ file with the *Apache License, Version 2.0* license for that library); - *E.g.* Artwork: <https://f-droid.org/about> (see the *CC BY-SA 3.0* license for artworks)"
msgstr ""
"Contoh:  \n"
"- *Secara umum:* <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/blob/master/LICENSE> (lisensi keseluruhan kode sumber di bawah *GPLv3+*).  \n"
"- *Header kode sumber:* <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/blob/master/app/src/main/java/org/fdroid/fdroid/AppDetails.java> (contoh header berkas dengan lisensi *GPLv3+*).  \n"
"- *Pustaka:* <https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/tree/master/libs> (lihat berkas _LICENSE_ dengan lisensi *Apache License Version 2.0* untuk pustaka tersebut).  \n"
"- *Karya seni:* <https://f-droid.org/about> (lihat lisensi *CC BY-SA 3.0* untuk unsur artistik)."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "All apps in the F-Droid repository *must* be FOSS (Free and Open Source software). If the software doesn't clearly state a license that is listed as a Free Software License in the [GNU license list](http://www.gnu.org/licenses/license-list.html#SoftwareLicenses)  then it probably isn't."
msgstr ""
"Semua aplikasi di repositori F-Droid *harus* bersifat FOSS (Free and Open Source Software).  \n"
"Jika perangkat lunak tidak secara jelas menyatakan lisensi yang terdaftar sebagai *Free Software License* di [daftar lisensi GNU](http://www.gnu.org/licenses/license-list.html#SoftwareLicenses), maka kemungkinan besar perangkat lunak tersebut tidak memenuhi kriteria."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "If there aren't any _README_ or _LICENSE_ in the source code of the app it's very difficult for the F-Droid community verify that the entire source code, libraries and artwork each are released under a suitable Free and Open Source license. So, it's a good pratice to verify that the app has headers in every file of the source code, a text file in the library folder and a statement in the source code or on the official website of the app that clearly explain the license about all the stuff that can be find related the app."
msgstr "Jika tidak ada _README_ atau _LICENSE_ di source code aplikasi, sangat sulit bagi komunitas F-Droid untuk memverifikasi bahwa seluruh source code, library, dan artwork masing-masing dirilis di bawah lisensi Free and Open Source yang sesuai. Karena itu, merupakan praktik yang baik untuk memeriksa bahwa aplikasi memiliki header di setiap file source code, sebuah file teks di folder library, dan pernyataan di source code atau di situs web resmi aplikasi yang dengan jelas menjelaskan lisensi untuk semua hal yang dapat ditemukan terkait aplikasi tersebut."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Note:* There is a little precisation to do about the use of the *GNU\n"
"General Public License **v2***. The Android support library and most\n"
"other Android libraries are licensed under the *Apache Licence*. Due to\n"
"technical legal reasons, these can't be combined with the *GNU General\n"
"Public License **v2***. In case of an app released under the\n"
"*GPL**v2***, it is legally accepted only if the source code headers of\n"
"the app say «GPLv2 **or later**», then we can choose the overall licence\n"
"to be *GPL**v3*** (this because on the contrary the *GPL**v3*** is full\n"
"legally compatible with the Android support library and the others\n"
"libraries).\n"
msgstr "*Catatan:* Ada sedikit penjelasan tambahan mengenai penggunaan *GNU General Public License **v2***. Android support library dan sebagian besar library Android lainnya berlisensi *Apache Licence*. Karena alasan hukum teknis, hal-hal ini tidak dapat digabungkan dengan *GNU General Public License **v2***. Dalam kasus aplikasi yang dirilis di bawah *GPL**v2***, secara hukum hanya diterima jika header source code aplikasi menyatakan «GPLv2 **atau lebih baru**», maka kami dapat memilih lisensi keseluruhan menjadi *GPL**v3*** (karena sebaliknya *GPL**v3*** sepenuhnya kompatibel secara hukum dengan Android support library dan library lainnya).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summaries"
msgstr "Ringkasan"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "The summary should be the shortest possible thing that describes what the app does or enables the user to do, e.g. instead of \"E-mail client\" use \"Receive and send e-mails\"."
msgstr ""
"Ringkasan harus sesingkat dan sejelas mungkin dalam menggambarkan fungsi aplikasi atau apa yang dapat dilakukan pengguna dengannya.  \n"
"Misalnya, alih-alih menulis “Aplikasi klien email”, tulislah “Kirim dan terima email”."

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Descriptions"
msgstr "Deskripsi"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Descriptions should be written in an objective, neutral style, with at least the first paragraph devoted to describing what the application is and what features it has. This can be followed with concise help for specific features/problems, and links to external resources for more information. Additional information such as links to related/compatible/required (but not alternative) applications should also be included where appropriate."
msgstr ""
"Deskripsi harus ditulis dengan gaya yang netral dan objektif.  \n"
"Paragraf pertama harus menjelaskan apa aplikasi tersebut dan fitur-fitur apa yang disediakan.  \n"
"Setelah itu, Anda dapat menambahkan bantuan singkat untuk fitur tertentu atau menyertakan tautan ke sumber eksternal untuk informasi lebih lanjut.  \n"
"Informasi tambahan seperti tautan ke aplikasi terkait atau yang diperlukan (tetapi bukan alternatif) juga dapat ditambahkan jika relevan."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Some other notes:"
msgstr "Beberapa catatan tambahan:"

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Phrases like \"a note-taking app for Android\" should never appear.  Obviously it's for Android. Obviously it's an app."
msgstr "Hindari frasa seperti “aplikasi pencatat untuk Android” — jelas bahwa aplikasi tersebut dibuat untuk Android."

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Similary, don't say \"it's free software\" or \"it's open source\" because obviously it is."
msgstr "Demikian juga, jangan menulis “ini adalah perangkat lunak bebas” atau “ini adalah sumber terbuka” karena semua aplikasi di F-Droid sudah harus memenuhi kriteria ini."

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Do not include compatiblity-related notes in there (e.g.  \"for Android 2.3+\") because this is handled automatically. Only include compatibility notes when the client app doesn't automatically detect them."
msgstr ""
"Jangan mencantumkan informasi tentang kompatibilitas sistem (misalnya “untuk Android 2.3+”), karena hal ini ditangani secara otomatis.  \n"
"Kecuali jika aplikasi secara eksplisit tidak dapat dideteksi kompatibilitasnya oleh sistem F-Droid, barulah informasi tambahan tersebut boleh disertakan."

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "The summary will always be shown with the description, so avoid repeating it."
msgstr "Ringkasan selalu ditampilkan bersama deskripsi, jadi hindari pengulangan isi yang sama."

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "If there is anything different about the F-Droid build compared to a standard one, it should be described."
msgstr "Jika versi F-Droid dari suatu aplikasi memiliki perbedaan dibandingkan versi aslinya, sebutkan perbedaan tersebut dalam deskripsi."

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "There should never be anything written from the developer's point of view, e.g. \"I wrote this cat gallery app because I like cats\"."
msgstr "Deskripsi tidak boleh ditulis dari sudut pandang pengembang, misalnya “Saya membuat aplikasi galeri kucing ini karena saya suka kucing.”"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Other information worth mentioning are:"
msgstr "Informasi lain yang sebaiknya ditambahkan meliputi:"

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Does the app require root permissions?"
msgstr "Apakah aplikasi memerlukan izin root?"

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Can it interact with other apps?"
msgstr "Apakah aplikasi dapat berinteraksi dengan aplikasi lain?"

#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "How easy is it to use?"
msgstr "Seberapa mudah aplikasi digunakan?"

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Donations"
msgstr "Donasi"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Where a project accepts donations, the ideal donation link would be to a specific page that the project maintains for that purpose. If one doesn't exist, it's acceptable to just link to their page that has a donation icon or similar somewhere on it, but this doesn't create a good user experience when, for example, someone selects 'Donate' in the F-Droid client and then has to search a page for the details. Try to encourage the developers to create a dedicate page if possible."
msgstr ""
"Jika proyek menerima donasi, sebaiknya sertakan tautan menuju halaman donasi khusus yang disediakan oleh pengembang.  \n"
"Jika halaman tersebut tidak tersedia, boleh menautkan ke situs utama yang memiliki ikon atau tombol donasi — meski hal tersebut kurang ideal.  \n"
"Pengalaman pengguna jadi kurang baik bila seseorang memilih opsi “Donasi” di aplikasi F-Droid dan harus mencari sendiri informasi donasi di situs tersebut.  \n"
"Usahakan mendorong pengembang untuk membuat halaman donasi khusus bila memungkinkan."

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "AntiFeatures"
msgstr "AntiFeatures"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "In addition some software, even being Free and Open Source software, may do practices which can be considered undesirable and that we consider [_AntiFeatures_](https://monitor.f-droid.org/anti-features)\". Where possible the F-Droid community still include these applications in the repository but flagging and cataloging these antifeatures in order to warn users (on the F-Droid client and on the web repository browser) by any antifeatures present on the app. Even though software can be included in the F-Droid even with antifeatures, it is frequently the case that software with these antifeatures is actually not entirely FOSS (for example advertising and tracking user activity is often enabled via Non-Free binary libraries) compromising in this way the inclusion of the app in the F-Droid repository."
msgstr "Selain itu, beberapa perangkat lunak, meskipun Free dan Open Source software, dapat melakukan praktik yang dapat dianggap tidak diinginkan dan yang kami anggap sebagai [_AntiFeatures_](https://monitor.f-droid.org/anti-features)\". Jika memungkinkan, komunitas F-Droid tetap memasukkan aplikasi-aplikasi ini ke dalam repository, tetapi menandai dan mengatalogkan antifeature tersebut untuk memperingatkan pengguna (di F-Droid client dan pada web repository browser) tentang antifeature yang ada pada aplikasi tersebut. Walaupun perangkat lunak dapat disertakan di F-Droid bahkan dengan antifeature, sering kali perangkat lunak dengan antifeature ini sebenarnya tidak sepenuhnya FOSS (misalnya iklan dan pelacakan aktivitas pengguna sering diaktifkan melalui binary libraries non-free), sehingga dengan cara ini mengompromikan pemasukan aplikasi ke dalam repository F-Droid."

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Updating"
msgstr "Pembaruan"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "<https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/graphs/master>"
msgstr "<https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/graphs/master>"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "<https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/network/master>"
msgstr "<https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidclient/network/master>"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "<https://f-droid.org/news-and-reviews>"
msgstr "<https://f-droid.org/news-and-reviews>"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "Getting the app in the repository isn't the end of the story: we have to keep the versions, descriptions and URLs up-to-date."
msgstr "Mendapatkan aplikasi ke dalam repository bukanlah akhir cerita: kami harus menjaga agar versi, deskripsi, dan URL tetap mutakhir."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Repository_Style_Guide.md
msgid "The most important is to know when new versions are published. We have three automatic methods and one manual: from tags; checking the _AndroidManifest.xml_ at the most recent revision in the repository; and checking Google Play. If these won't do, we must look at the version of the package published by the upstream developers, either by loading the Google Play web page or downloading an APK and checking its version.  Repository tags are the natural way of labelling new versions (look for them under \"releases\" on an example in [github.com](https://github.com/dschuermann/document-viewer/releases) or under the \"tags\" directory in the case of SVN repos). If you can't find tags it would be a helpful to make an issue about it on the issue tracker. In the example, we point to a changelog page as a backup check; other possiblities are a Google Code download page or a Google Play link."
msgstr "Yang paling penting adalah mengetahui kapan versi baru dipublikasikan. Kami memiliki tiga metode otomatis dan satu manual: dari tag; memeriksa _AndroidManifest.xml_ pada revisi paling baru di repository; dan memeriksa Google Play. Jika itu tidak memadai, kami harus melihat versi paket yang dipublikasikan oleh pengembang upstream, baik dengan memuat halaman web Google Play atau mengunduh APK dan memeriksa versinya. Tag repository adalah cara alami untuk memberi label versi baru (lihat pada bagian _releases_ dalam contoh di [github.com](https://github.com/dschuermann/document-viewer/releases) atau pada direktori _tags_ untuk repo SVN). Jika Anda tidak dapat menemukan tag, akan sangat membantu untuk membuat issue tentang hal itu di issue tracker. Dalam contoh ini, kami menunjuk ke halaman changelog sebagai pemeriksaan cadangan; kemungkinan lain adalah halaman unduhan Google Code atau tautan Google Play."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reproducible Builds"
msgstr "Reproducible Builds"

#. type: Title ##
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md _docs/Take-Down_Requests.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Pendahuluan"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "F-Droid works to spread [reproducible builds](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/definition/) across the free software Android ecosystem.  The goal is to enable software build processes that anyone can run repeatedly and reproduce the exact same APK as the original release.  Our work is focused on three main areas:"
msgstr "F-Droid bekerja untuk menyebarkan [reproducible builds](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/definition/) di seluruh ekosistem Android free software. Tujuannya adalah memungkinkan proses build perangkat lunak yang dapat dijalankan siapa pun berulang kali dan menghasilkan APK yang persis sama dengan rilis asli. Pekerjaan kami berfokus pada tiga area utama:"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Our [build environment](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidserver/-/tree/master/buildserver) is designed to make reproducing builds easy while being itself reproducible and auditable."
msgstr "[build environment](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidserver/-/tree/master/buildserver) kami dirancang untuk memudahkan reproduksi build sekaligus tetap dapat direproduksi dan diaudit."

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "We track issues in the build tools themselves that prevent reproducible builds, help the maintainers of the build tools fix these issues, and catalogue workarounds for app developers here in this web page."
msgstr "Kami melacak issue pada build tools itu sendiri yang menghalangi reproducible builds, membantu maintainer build tools memperbaiki issue ini, dan mengatalogkan workaround bagi developer aplikasi di halaman web ini."

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "We help upstream app developers for any app shipped on <tt>f-droid.org</tt> fix issues with reproducible builds by providing developer support, filing issues and suggesting changes to the source code."
msgstr "Kami membantu developer upstream untuk aplikasi apa pun yang dikirim di <tt>f-droid.org</tt> memperbaiki masalah reproducible builds dengan memberikan dukungan developer, membuka issue, dan menyarankan perubahan pada source code."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "F-Droid verifies reproducible builds using APK [signature copying](#reproducible-signatures) against upstream build and our rebuild. To find out if an app can be reproducibly rebuilt by our own buildserver, check the \"[Reproducibility Status](https://f-droid.org/packages/org.fdroid.fdroid/#reproducibility_status)\" on any app's page on this website. This can help us identify factors changing over time."
msgstr "F-Droid memverifikasi reproducible builds menggunakan APK [signature copying](#reproducible-signatures) terhadap build upstream dan rebuild kami. Untuk mengetahui apakah sebuah aplikasi dapat dibangun ulang secara reproducible oleh buildserver kami, periksa \"[Reproducibility Status](https://f-droid.org/packages/org.fdroid.fdroid/#reproducibility_status)\" pada halaman aplikasi mana pun di situs ini. Ini dapat membantu kami mengidentifikasi faktor yang berubah seiring waktu."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "The gold standard in reproducible builds for countering [Trusting Trust](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~rdriley/487/papers/Thompson_1984_ReflectionsonTrustingTrust.pdf) issues is [Diverse Double-Compiling](https://dwheeler.com/trusting-trust/). The core idea is to use two entirely distinct sets of build tools to create the exact same binary.  This is a difficult standard to achieve, although quite valuable.  Some of the work to get there can be done incrementally.  Towards that end, F-Droid can reproduce the APKs that the upstream developer built on their own setup.  Often times, these are built with different toolchains or on different OSes.  To see which apps have enabled this approach, please check its [build metadata](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/blob/master/metadata/{packageName}.yml) for the presence of build metadata fields [`Binaries:`](https://f-droid.org/docs/Build_Metadata_Reference/#Binaries) or [`binary:`](https://f-droid.org/docs/Build_Metadata_Reference/#build_binary)."
msgstr "Standar emas dalam reproducible builds untuk menangkal masalah [Trusting Trust](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~rdriley/487/papers/Thompson_1984_ReflectionsonTrustingTrust.pdf) adalah [Diverse Double-Compiling](https://dwheeler.com/trusting-trust/). Gagasan utamanya adalah menggunakan dua set build tools yang sepenuhnya berbeda untuk menghasilkan binary yang persis sama. Ini merupakan standar yang sulit dicapai, meskipun sangat berharga. Sebagian pekerjaan untuk mencapainya dapat dilakukan secara bertahap. Ke arah itu, F-Droid dapat mereproduksi APK yang dibangun pengembang upstream pada setup mereka sendiri. Sering kali, build ini menggunakan toolchain atau OS yang berbeda. Untuk melihat aplikasi mana yang telah mengaktifkan pendekatan ini, silakan periksa [build metadata](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/blob/master/metadata/{packageName}.yml) untuk keberadaan field metadata build [`Binaries:`](https://f-droid.org/docs/Build_Metadata_Reference/#Binaries) atau [`binary:`](https://f-droid.org/docs/Build_Metadata_Reference/#build_binary)."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reproducible signatures"
msgstr "Reproducible signatures"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "F-Droid verifies reproducible builds using the [APK signature](https://source.android.com/docs/security/features/apksigning)  (a form of [embedded signature](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/embedded-signatures/)), which requires [copying](https://github.com/obfusk/apksigcopier) the signature from a signed APK to an unsigned one and then checking if the latter verifies.  The old v1 (JAR) signatures only cover the *contents* of the APK (e.g. ZIP metadata and ordering are irrelevant), but v2/v3 signatures cover *all other bytes in the APK*.  Thus, the APKs must be completely identical *before* and *after* signing (apart from the signature) in order to verify correctly."
msgstr ""
"F-Droid memverifikasi *reproducible builds* menggunakan [*tanda tangan APK (APK signature)*](https://source.android.com/docs/security/features/apksigning) — sebuah bentuk dari [*tanda tangan tertanam (embedded signature)*](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/embedded-signatures/) — dengan cara [menyalin](https://github.com/obfusk/apksigcopier) tanda tangan dari APK bertanda tangan ke APK tidak bertanda tangan, lalu memverifikasinya.  \n"
"Tanda tangan versi lama (v1 / JAR) hanya mencakup *isi* APK, sehingga metadata ZIP dan urutan file diabaikan.  \n"
"Namun, tanda tangan versi baru (v2/v3) mencakup seluruh byte dalam APK.  \n"
"Artinya, untaian byte APK harus identik *sebelum* dan *sesudah* proses penandatanganan agar dapat diverifikasi dengan benar."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Copying the signature uses the same algorithm that `apksigner` uses when signing an APK.  It is therefore important that (upstream) developers do the same when signing APKs, ideally by using `apksigner` to make the signatures.  `apksigner` is also reproducibly built [in Debian](https://tests.reproducible-builds.org/debian/rb-pkg/trixie/amd64/android-platform-tools-apksig.html)."
msgstr "Penyalinan signature menggunakan algoritma yang sama dengan yang digunakan `apksigner` saat menandatangani APK. Karena itu, penting agar pengembang (upstream) melakukan hal yang sama saat menandatangani APK, idealnya dengan menggunakan `apksigner` untuk membuat signature. `apksigner` juga direproduksi secara reproducible [di Debian](https://tests.reproducible-builds.org/debian/rb-pkg/trixie/amd64/android-platform-tools-apksig.html)."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verification builds"
msgstr "Verification builds"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Many people or organizations will be interested in reproducing builds to make sure that the f-droid.org builds match the original source and nothing has been modified.  In that case, the resulting APKs are not published for installation.  The [Verification Server](../Verification_Server) automates this process."
msgstr ""
"Banyak individu atau organisasi tertarik untuk mereproduksi proses build agar memastikan bahwa build dari f-droid.org benar-benar sesuai dengan kode sumber aslinya dan tidak dimodifikasi.  \n"
"Dalam kasus seperti ini, APK hasil verifikasi tidak diterbitkan untuk instalasi publik.  \n"
"[Server Verifikasi](../Verification_Server) mengotomatiskan proses ini."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Situation"
msgstr "Situasi"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Quite a few builds already verify with no extra effort since Java code is often compiled into the same bytecode by a wide range of Java versions.  The Android SDK's `build-tools` will create differences in the resulting XML, PNG, etc.  files, but this is usually not a problem since the `build.gradle` includes the exact version of `build-tools` to use."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar build sudah dapat diverifikasi tanpa usaha ekstra karena kode Java umumnya dikompilasi menjadi bytecode yang identik di berbagai versi Java.  \n"
"Alat `build-tools` dalam Android SDK dapat menghasilkan perbedaan kecil pada berkas XML, PNG, dan lainnya, namun ini biasanya tidak masalah karena berkas `build.gradle` menentukan versi tepat dari `build-tools` yang digunakan."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Anything built using the NDK will be much more sensitive.  For example, even for builds that use the exact same version of the NDK (e.g. `r13b`) but on different platforms (e.g. macOS versus Ubuntu), the resulting binaries will have differences."
msgstr "Apa pun yang dibangun menggunakan NDK akan jauh lebih sensitif. Misalnya, bahkan untuk build yang menggunakan versi NDK yang sama persis (misalnya `r13b`) tetapi pada platform yang berbeda (misalnya macOS versus Ubuntu), binary yang dihasilkan akan memiliki perbedaan."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Additionally, we'll have to look out for anything that includes timestamps or build paths, is sensitive to sort order, etc."
msgstr "Selain itu, kita perlu memperhatikan apa pun yang menyertakan timestamp atau build path, yang sensitif terhadap urutan sort, dan sebagainya."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Google is also working towards reproducible builds of Android apps, so using recent versions of the Android SDK helps.  One specific case is starting with Gradle Android Plugin v2.2.2, timestamps in the APK file's ZIP metadata are automatically zeroed out."
msgstr "Google juga sedang bekerja menuju reproducible builds untuk aplikasi Android, jadi menggunakan versi Android SDK yang terbaru akan membantu. Salah satu kasus khusus adalah mulai dari Gradle Android Plugin v2.2.2, timestamp dalam metadata ZIP file APK secara otomatis di-nolkan."

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Publishing APKs with the upstream developer's signature"
msgstr "Menerbitkan APK dengan tanda tangan dari pengembang asli"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "An application can be setup to publish the signed binaries from the upstream developer after verifying that they match the ones built using an _fdroiddata_ build recipe.  Publishing only takes place if there is a proper match. This means that F-Droid can verify that an app is free software while still using the original developer's APK signatures. This procedure is implemented as part of [`fdroid publish`](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidserver/-/blob/master/fdroidserver/publish.py).  The reproducibility check at the publishing step follows this logic:"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah aplikasi dapat dikonfigurasikan agar menerbitkan biner bertanda tangan dari pengembang hulu setelah memastikan bahwa hasil tersebut cocok dengan hasil build yang dihasilkan melalui resep build di _fdroiddata_.  \n"
"Proses penerbitan hanya dilakukan jika hasil cocok secara sempurna.  \n"
"Dengan demikian, F-Droid dapat memverifikasi bahwa aplikasi benar-benar bebas sambil tetap menggunakan tanda tangan asli pengembang.  \n"
"Prosedur ini diimplementasikan melalui perintah [`fdroid publish`](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroidserver/-/blob/master/fdroidserver/publish.py).  \n"
"Pemeriksaan reproduktibilitas di tahap penerbitan mengikuti logika berikut:"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "![Flow-chart for reproducibility check]({% asset docs/reproducible-builds/publish.png %})"
msgstr "![Diagram alur pemeriksaan reproduktibilitas]({% asset docs/reproducible-builds/publish.png %})"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exclusively publishing (upstream) developer-signed APKs"
msgstr "Menerbitkan hanya APK yang ditandatangani oleh pengembang (hulu)"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "For this approach, everything in the metadata should be the same as normal, with the addition of the [`Binaries`](../Build_Metadata_Reference/#Binaries) or [`Builds.binary`](../Build_Metadata_Reference/#build_binary) directive to specify where to get the binaries (APKs) from, and [`AllowedAPKSigningKeys`](../Build_Metadata_Reference/#AllowedAPKSigningKeys) directive to ensure the expected signing key is used. In this case, F-Droid will never attempt to publish APKs signed by F-Droid.  If `fdroid publish` can verify that the downloaded APK matches the one built from the _fdroiddata_ recipe, the downloaded APK will be published. Otherwise F-Droid will skip publishing this version of the app."
msgstr ""
"Untuk metode ini, metadata aplikasi sama seperti biasa, dengan tambahan direktif [`Binaries`](../Build_Metadata_Reference/#Binaries) atau [`Builds.binary`](../Build_Metadata_Reference/#build_binary) untuk menentukan lokasi biner (APK) serta direktif [`AllowedAPKSigningKeys`](../Build_Metadata_Reference/#AllowedAPKSigningKeys) untuk memastikan kunci tanda tangan yang digunakan sudah sesuai.  \n"
"\n"
"Dalam konfigurasi ini, F-Droid tidak akan pernah mencoba menerbitkan APK yang ditandatangani oleh F-Droid sendiri.  \n"
"Jika `fdroid publish` berhasil memverifikasi bahwa APK yang diunduh identik dengan hasil build dari resep _fdroiddata_, maka APK tersebut akan diterbitkan.  \n"
"Jika tidak, versi aplikasi tersebut akan dilewati."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Publish both (upstream) developer-signed and F-Droid-signed APKs"
msgstr "Menerbitkan APK yang ditandatangani oleh pengembang (hulu) dan F-Droid"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "This approach allows publishing both APKs signed by the (upstream) developer and APKs signed by F-Droid.  This enables us to ship updates for users who installed apps from other sources than F-Droid (e.g. Play Store), while also shipping updates for apps which were built and signed by F-Droid."
msgstr ""
"Pendekatan ini memungkinkan penerbitan dua versi:  \n"
"APK bertanda tangan pengembang hulu dan APK bertanda tangan F-Droid.  \n"
"Hal ini memungkinkan F-Droid mengirimkan pembaruan untuk pengguna yang memasang aplikasi dari sumber lain (seperti Play Store), sekaligus menyediakan pembaruan untuk versi yang dibangun sepenuhnya oleh F-Droid."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "This requires extracting and adding (upstream) developer signatures to _fdroiddata_.  These signatures are then later copied to the unsigned APK built from the _fdroiddata_ recipe.  We provide a command for easily extracting signatures from APKs:"
msgstr ""
"Proses ini memerlukan ekstraksi tanda tangan pengembang hulu dan menambahkannya ke data _fdroiddata_.  \n"
"Tanda tangan tersebut kemudian disalin ke APK tanpa tanda tangan yang dihasilkan dari resep build.  \n"
"F-Droid menyediakan perintah untuk mengekstrak tanda tangan dari APK dengan mudah:"

#. type: Fenced code block (console)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cd /path/to/fdroiddata\n"
"$ fdroid signatures F-Droid.apk\n"
msgstr ""
"$ cd /path/to/fdroiddata\n"
"$ fdroid signatures F-Droid.apk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Instead of local files, you can also supply HTTPS URLs to `fdroid signatures`."
msgstr "Alih-alih file lokal, Anda juga dapat menyediakan URL HTTPS ke `fdroid signatures`."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "The signature files are extracted to the app's metadata directory, ready to be used with `fdroid publish`.  A signature consists of 2-6 files: a v1 signature (manifest, signature file, and signature block file) and/or a v2/v3 signature (APK Signing Block and offset); if the APK was v1-signed with e.g.  `signflinger` instead of `apksigner` there will also be a `differences.json`.  The result of extracting one will resemble these file listings:"
msgstr "File signature diekstrak ke direktori metadata aplikasi, siap digunakan dengan `fdroid publish`. Sebuah signature terdiri dari 2-6 file: signature v1 (manifest, signature file, dan signature block file) dan/atau signature v2/v3 (APK Signing Block dan offset); jika APK ditandatangani v1 misalnya dengan `signflinger` alih-alih `apksigner` maka juga akan ada `differences.json`. Hasil dari ekstraksi salah satunya akan menyerupai daftar file berikut:"

#. type: Fenced code block (console)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ ls metadata/org.fdroid.fdroid/signatures/1000012/  # v1 signature only\n"
"CIARANG.RSA  CIARANG.SF  MANIFEST.MF\n"
"$ ls metadata/your.app/signatures/42/                # v1 + v2/v3 signature\n"
"APKSigningBlock  APKSigningBlockOffset  MANIFEST.MF  YOURKEY.RSA  YOURKEY.SF\n"
msgstr ""
"$ ls metadata/org.fdroid.fdroid/signatures/1000012/  # v1 signature only\n"
"CIARANG.RSA  CIARANG.SF  MANIFEST.MF\n"
"$ ls metadata/your.app/signatures/42/                # v1 + v2/v3 signature\n"
"APKSigningBlock  APKSigningBlockOffset  MANIFEST.MF  YOURKEY.RSA  YOURKEY.SF\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tools"
msgstr "Alat"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diffing the apk"
msgstr "Diffing the apk"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "We recommend using [`diffoscope`](https://diffoscope.org/) for easily finding the difference between the reference APK provided by the app developer and the APK that `fdroidserver` produced."
msgstr "Kami merekomendasikan penggunaan [`diffoscope`](https://diffoscope.org/) untuk dengan mudah menemukan perbedaan antara APK referensi yang disediakan oleh developer aplikasi dan APK yang dihasilkan `fdroidserver`."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "You can find the APK that `fdroidserver` produced either under e.g.  `fdroiddata/build/com.example.app/app/build/outputs/apk/prod/release/example-1.0.0-prod-release-unsigned.apk` (when running locally) or in the pipeline artefacts (when using GitLab CI).  Adjust the path accordingly (e.g. for flavours other than `prod`)."
msgstr "Anda dapat menemukan APK yang dihasilkan `fdroidserver` baik di misalnya `fdroiddata/build/com.example.app/app/build/outputs/apk/prod/release/example-1.0.0-prod-release-unsigned.apk` (saat dijalankan secara lokal) atau di artefak pipeline (saat menggunakan GitLab CI). Sesuaikan path-nya sebagaimana mestinya (misalnya untuk flavour selain `prod`)."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prioritising & fixing differences"
msgstr "Prioritising & fixing differences"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "[HOWTO: diff & fix APKs for Reproducible Builds](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/wiki/-/wikis/HOWTO:-diff-&-fix-APKs-for-Reproducible-Builds)  on the F-Droid wiki has detailed information on the various kinds of differences commonly encountered, which differences should usually be prioritised when debugging, and how to fix common issues."
msgstr "Panduan [HOWTO: diff & fix APKs for Reproducible Builds](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/wiki/-/wikis/HOWTO:-diff-&-fix-APKs-for-Reproducible-Builds) di wiki F-Droid menjelaskan secara mendalam jenis perbedaan yang umum terjadi, perbedaan mana yang harus lebih diprioritaskan saat debugging, serta cara mengatasi permasalahan umum tersebut."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "It also shows how to use various specialised tools that may provide better results when `diffoscope` is not sufficient."
msgstr "Dokumen ini juga menunjukkan cara menggunakan berbagai alat khusus yang mungkin memberikan hasil lebih baik saat `diffoscope` tidak cukup."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reproducible APK tools"
msgstr "Alat APK yang reproducible"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, fuzzy
msgid "The scripts from [reproducible-apk-tools](https://github.com/obfusk/reproducible-apk-tools)  (available in _fdroiddata_ as a `srclib`) may help to make builds reproducible, e.g. by fixing newlines (CRLF vs LF) or making ZIP ordering deterministic, if removing the cause of the differences is not a realistic option.  Depending on specifics, these scripts need to be used by upstream developers before signing their APKs, by the _fdroiddata_ recipe, or both."
msgstr ""
"Skrip dari proyek [reproducible-apk-tools](https://github.com/obfusk/reproducible-apk-tools) (tersedia di *fdroiddata* sebagai `srclib`) dapat membantu membuat build menjadi lebih konsisten — misalnya dengan memperbaiki format akhir baris (*newline*: CRLF vs LF) atau membuat urutan dalam file ZIP menjadi deterministik.  \n"
"Jika penyebab perbedaannya tidak realistis untuk dihilangkan, skrip ini bisa dijalankan oleh pengembang hulu sebelum menandatangani APK, oleh resep *fdroiddata*, atau keduanya."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Originally created to inject non-determinism in build processes, [disorderfs](https://salsa.debian.org/reproducible-builds/disorderfs) can also do the opposite: make reading from the filesystem deterministic.  In some cases this can make e.g. `resources.arsc` reproducible.  Here is an example from an existing recipe:"
msgstr "Awalnya dibuat untuk menyuntikkan non-determinisme ke dalam proses build, [disorderfs](https://salsa.debian.org/reproducible-builds/disorderfs) juga dapat melakukan kebalikannya: membuat pembacaan dari filesystem menjadi deterministik. Dalam beberapa kasus ini dapat membuat misalnya `resources.arsc` menjadi reproducible. Berikut contoh dari recipe yang sudah ada:"

#. type: Fenced code block (console)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ mv my.app my.app_underlying\n"
"$ disorderfs --sort-dirents=yes --reverse-dirents=no my.app_underlying my.app\n"
msgstr ""
"$ mv my.app my.app_underlying\n"
"$ disorderfs --sort-dirents=yes --reverse-dirents=no my.app_underlying my.app\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Potential sources of unreproducible builds"
msgstr "Potential sources of unreproducible builds"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "There are various ways builds can be unreproducible.  Some are relatively easy to avoid, others are hard to fix.  We've tried to list some common sources below."
msgstr ""
"Terdapat berbagai faktor yang dapat menyebabkan build tidak dapat direproduksi.  \n"
"Beberapa di antaranya mudah dihindari, tetapi sebagian lainnya cukup sulit diperbaiki.  \n"
"Berikut adalah beberapa penyebab umum yang ditemui:"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "See also [this GitLab issue](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/issues/2816)."
msgstr "Lihat juga [masalah GitLab ini](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/issues/2816)."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bug: Android Studio builds have non-deterministic ZIP ordering"
msgstr "Bug: Android Studio menghasilkan urutan ZIP yang tidak deterministik"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "[Non-deterministic order of ZIP entries in APK makes builds not reproducible](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/265653160)  (may require a Google account to view)."
msgstr "[Urutan entry ZIP yang tidak deterministik dalam APK membuat build tidak reproducible](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/265653160)  (mungkin memerlukan akun Google untuk melihat)."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "NB: this should be fixed in Android Gradle plugin (`com.android.tools.build:gradle` / `com.android.application`) `7.1.X` and later."
msgstr "NB: ini seharusnya sudah diperbaiki di Android Gradle plugin (`com.android.tools.build:gradle` / `com.android.application`) `7.1.X` dan yang lebih baru."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, fuzzy
msgid "When building APKs with Android Studio, the ordering of the ZIP entries in the APK can be different from that of APKs built by invoking `gradle` directly, affecting reproducibility; the ordering can be completely non-deterministic, even differing between different builds of the same source code."
msgstr "Saat membangun APK menggunakan Android Studio, urutan *entry* dalam struktur ZIP dapat berbeda dibandingkan dengan APK yang dibangun langsung menggunakan `gradle`. Hal ini memengaruhi reproducibility karena urutan file bisa benar-benar acak, bahkan antar build dari sumber kode yang sama."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "A workaround for older versions is to invoke `gradle` directly (as during F-Droid or CI builds), bypassing Android Studio:"
msgstr "Solusi untuk versi yang lebih lama adalah memanggil `gradle` secara langsung (seperti saat build F-Droid atau CI), melewati Android Studio:"

#. type: Fenced code block (console)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ./gradlew assembleRelease\n"
msgstr "$ ./gradlew assembleRelease\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "NB: depending on your signing configuration, this may require signing the APK with `apksigner` afterwards, since signing is not performed by Android Studio in this case."
msgstr "Catatan: tergantung pada konfigurasi penandatanganan Anda, mungkin perlu menandatangani APK menggunakan `apksigner` setelah proses build selesai, karena Android Studio tidak melakukan penandatanganan otomatis dalam metode ini."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "`apksigner` from build-tools >= 35.0.0-rc1 outputs unverifiable APKs"
msgstr "`apksigner` dari build-tools >= 35.0.0-rc1 menghasilkan APK yang tidak dapat diverifikasi"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Using `apksigner` from build-tools version 34 produces APKs verifiable by `apksigcopier`, but newer versions will fail.  We are tracking this issue in [#3299](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/issues/3299) and there's more info in [apksigcopier issues 105](https://github.com/obfusk/apksigcopier/issues/105). Github Actions CI Ubuntu images starting July 2024 have version 35 included, so one needs to manually select the `apksigner` version from 34 instead of the default templated \"latest version\"."
msgstr "Menggunakan `apksigner` dari build-tools versi 34 menghasilkan APK yang dapat diverifikasi oleh `apksigcopier`, tetapi versi yang lebih baru akan gagal. Kami sedang melacak isu ini di [#3299](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/fdroiddata/-/issues/3299) dan ada info lebih lanjut di [apksigcopier issues 105](https://github.com/obfusk/apksigcopier/issues/105). Image CI Ubuntu GitHub yang mulai Juli 2024 sudah menyertakan versi 35, jadi perlu memilih versi `apksigner` dari 34 secara manual alih-alih default templat \"versi terbaru\"."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bug: baseline.prof not deterministic"
msgstr "Bug: baseline.prof tidak deterministik"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Sometimes the `baselin.prof` file is not reproducible. There are some possible workarounds:"
msgstr "Kadang-kadang file `baselin.prof` tidak reproducible. Ada beberapa solusi yang mungkin:"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Rerun the build until the file matches."
msgstr "Jalankan ulang build sampai file cocok."

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Use the same CPU core number as upstream."
msgstr "Gunakan jumlah core CPU yang sama seperti upstream."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Disable the baseline profile.\n"
"  Add this to `build.gradle`:\n"
msgstr ""
"1. Nonaktifkan baseline profile.\n"
"   Tambahkan ini ke `build.gradle`:\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  tasks.whenTaskAdded { task ->\n"
"      if (task.name.contains(\"ArtProfile\")) {\n"
"          task.enabled = false\n"
"      }\n"
"  }\n"
msgstr ""
"  tasks.whenTaskAdded { task ->\n"
"      if (task.name.contains(\"ArtProfile\")) {\n"
"          task.enabled = false\n"
"      }\n"
"  }\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "  or this to `build.gradle.kts`:\n"
msgstr "  atau ini ke `build.gradle.kts`:\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (kotlin)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  tasks.whenTaskAdded {\n"
"    if (name.contains(\"ArtProfile\")) {\n"
"        enabled = false\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"
msgstr ""
"  tasks.whenTaskAdded {\n"
"    if (name.contains(\"ArtProfile\")) {\n"
"        enabled = false\n"
"    }\n"
"  }\n"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bug: baseline.profm not deterministic"
msgstr "Bug: baseline.profm tidak deterministik"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "[Non-stable `assets/dexopt/baseline.profm`](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/231837768)  (may require a Google account to view)."
msgstr "[Non-stable `assets/dexopt/baseline.profm`](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/231837768) (mungkin memerlukan akun Google untuk dilihat)."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "See also [this write-up of workarounds](https://gist.github.com/obfusk/61046e09cee352ae6dd109911534b12e)."
msgstr "Lihat juga [tulisan ini tentang workaround](https://gist.github.com/obfusk/61046e09cee352ae6dd109911534b12e)."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bug: coreLibraryDesugaring not deterministic"
msgstr "Bug: coreLibraryDesugaring tidak deterministik"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "NB: this should be fixed in R8 (`com.android.tools:r8`) `3.0.69` and later."
msgstr "Catatan: masalah ini telah diperbaiki di R8 (`com.android.tools:r8`) versi `3.0.69` dan yang lebih baru."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "In some cases builds are not reproducible due to a [bug in `coreLibraryDesugaring`](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/195968520)  (may require a Google account to view); this [affected NewPipe](https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipe/issues/6486)."
msgstr "Dalam beberapa kasus build tidak reproducible karena [bug di `coreLibraryDesugaring`](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/195968520) (mungkin memerlukan akun Google untuk melihat); hal ini [mempengaruhi NewPipe](https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipe/issues/6486)."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bug: line ending differences between Windows and Linux builds"
msgstr "Bug: perbedaan line ending antara build Windows dan Linux"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "[Newline differences between building on Windows vs Linux make builds not reproducible](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/266109851)  (may require a Google account to view)."
msgstr "[Perbedaan newline antara build di Windows dan Linux membuat build tidak reproducible](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/266109851)  (mungkin memerlukan akun Google untuk melihatnya)."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "A workaround is to run [`fix-newlines.py`](https://github.com/obfusk/reproducible-apk-tools#fix-newlinespy)  on the *unsigned* APK with the \"wrong\" line endings to change them from LF to CRLF (or vice versa w/ `--from-crlf`) and `zipalign` it again afterwards."
msgstr "Workaround-nya adalah menjalankan [`fix-newlines.py`](https://github.com/obfusk/reproducible-apk-tools#fix-newlinespy) pada APK *unsigned* dengan line ending yang \"salah\" untuk mengubahnya dari LF ke CRLF (atau sebaliknya dengan `--from-crlf`) lalu menjalankan `zipalign` lagi setelahnya."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Concurrency: reproducibility can depend on the number of CPUs/cores"
msgstr "Concurrency: reproducibility dapat bergantung pada jumlah CPU/core"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "This can affect `.dex` files (though that seems to be rare) or native code (e.g.  Rust)."
msgstr "Kondisi ini dapat memengaruhi berkas `.dex` (meskipun jarang terjadi) atau kode native seperti Rust."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Using only 1 CPU/core as a workaround:"
msgstr "Menggunakan hanya 1 CPU/core sebagai workaround:"

#. type: Fenced code block (console)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"export CPUS_MAX=1\n"
"export CPUS=$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN)\n"
"for (( c=$CPUS_MAX; c<$CPUS; c++ )) ; do echo 0 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu$c/online; done\n"
msgstr ""
"export CPUS_MAX=1\n"
"export CPUS=$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN)\n"
"for (( c=$CPUS_MAX; c<$CPUS; c++ )) ; do echo 0 > /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu$c/online; done\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "NB: this workaround affects the entire machine, so using it in a non-persistent virtual machine or container is recommended."
msgstr "Catatan: solusi ini memengaruhi seluruh sistem, jadi sebaiknya digunakan pada mesin virtual atau kontainer sementara untuk menghindari gangguan permanen."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "For Rust code, you can set [`codegen-units = 1`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/codegen-options/index.html#codegen-units)."
msgstr "Untuk kode Rust, Anda dapat mengatur [`codegen-units = 1`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/codegen-options/index.html#codegen-units)."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "See also [this GitLab issue](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/rfp/-/issues/1519#note_1226216164)."
msgstr "Lihat juga [issue GitLab ini](https://gitlab.com/fdroid/rfp/-/issues/1519#note_1226216164)."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embedded build paths"
msgstr "Embedded build paths"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Embedded [build paths](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/build-path/) are a source of reproducibility issues affecting apps built with e.g. Flutter, python-for-android, or using native code (e.g. Rust, C/C++, any kind of `libfoo.so`).  Apps completely written in Java and/or Kotlin tend to be unaffected."
msgstr "Embedded [build paths](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/build-path/) merupakan sumber masalah reproducibility yang memengaruhi aplikasi yang dibangun dengan misalnya Flutter, python-for-android, atau yang menggunakan native code (misalnya Rust, C/C++, jenis apa pun `libfoo.so`). Aplikasi yang sepenuhnya ditulis dalam Java dan/atau Kotlin cenderung tidak terpengaruh."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Often, the easiest solution is to always use the same working directory when building; e.g. `/builds/fdroid/fdroiddata/build/your.app.id` (F-Droid CI), `/home/vagrant/build/your.app.id` (F-Droid build server), `/tmp/build` or create one to mirror the upstream used folders, e.g. for macOS `/Users/runner`."
msgstr "Cara termudah untuk menghindarinya adalah dengan selalu menggunakan direktori kerja yang sama saat melakukan build — misalnya: `/builds/fdroid/fdroiddata/build/your.app.id` (F-Droid CI), `/home/vagrant/build/your.app.id` (server build F-Droid), atau `/tmp/build`, atau buat direktori yang menyerupai jalur build di sistem pengembang hulu, misalnya di macOS: `/Users/runner`."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "NB: using a subdirectory of the world-writeable `/tmp` can have security implications (on multi-user systems)."
msgstr "Catatan: menggunakan subdirektori di dalam `/tmp` yang dapat ditulis oleh semua pengguna memiliki potensi risiko keamanan pada sistem multi-pengguna."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the SDK path ends up embedded in Flutter one can move the SDK to said path\n"
"in the recipe and configure it with: `flutter config --android-sdk <path>` as\n"
"setting `ANDROID_SDK_ROOT` might not be enough.\n"
msgstr "Jika path SDK akhirnya tertanam di Flutter, Anda dapat memindahkan SDK ke path tersebut dalam recipe dan mengonfigurasinya dengan: `flutter config --android-sdk <path>` karena mengatur `ANDROID_SDK_ROOT` mungkin tidak cukup.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "If the lib is not stripped properly, then debug info may be kept which usually has many paths. Enable strip can remove them. This can be done by setting NDK version correctly or pass `-s` to the linker. This can also be done manually, e.g., using `llvm-strip`."
msgstr "Jika library tidak di-strip dengan benar, maka debug info mungkin tetap ada yang biasanya memiliki banyak path. Mengaktifkan strip dapat menghapusnya. Hal ini dapat dilakukan dengan mengatur versi NDK dengan benar atau memberikan `-s` ke linker. Hal ini juga dapat dilakukan secara manual, misalnya dengan `llvm-strip`."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embedded timestamps"
msgstr "Timestamp yang tertanam"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Embedded [timestamps](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/timestamps/) are the most common source of reproducibility issues and are best avoided."
msgstr "[Timestamps](https://reproducible-builds.org/docs/timestamps/) yang tertanam adalah sumber masalah reproducibility yang paling umum dan sebaiknya dihindari."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Native library stripping"
msgstr "Native library stripping"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "It seems that the stripping of native libraries, e.g. `libfoo.so`, can cause intermittent reproducibility issues.  It is important to use the exact NDK version when rebuilding, e.g. `r21e`.  Disabling stripping can sometimes help.  Gradle seems to strip shared libraries by default, even the app is receiving the shared libraries via an AAR library.  Here is how to disable it in Gradle:"
msgstr "Tampaknya stripping pada native libraries, misalnya `libfoo.so`, dapat menyebabkan masalah reproducibility yang muncul-tenggelam. Penting untuk menggunakan versi NDK yang persis sama saat membangun ulang, misalnya `r21e`. Menonaktifkan stripping terkadang dapat membantu. Gradle tampaknya melakukan strip shared libraries secara bawaan, bahkan ketika aplikasi menerima shared libraries tersebut melalui library AAR. Berikut cara menonaktifkannya di Gradle:"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"android {\n"
"    packagingOptions {\n"
"        doNotStrip '**/*.so'\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"android {\n"
"    packagingOptions {\n"
"        doNotStrip '**/*.so'\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "NDK _build-id_"
msgstr "NDK _build-id_"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "On different build machines, different NDK paths and different paths to the project (and thus to its `jni` directory) are used.  This leads to different paths to the source files in debug symbols, causing the linker to generate a different _build-id_, which is preserved after stripping."
msgstr "Pada mesin build yang berbeda, digunakan path NDK yang berbeda dan path ke project (dan karena itu ke direktori `jni`-nya) yang berbeda. Hal ini menyebabkan path ke source file di debug symbols berbeda, sehingga linker menghasilkan _build-id_ yang berbeda, yang dipertahankan setelah stripping."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "One possible solution is passing `--build-id=none` to the linker which will disable _build-id_ generation completely."
msgstr "Salah satu solusi yang mungkin adalah dengan meneruskan `--build-id=none` ke linker yang akan menonaktifkan pembuatan _build-id_ sepenuhnya."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "NDK hash style"
msgstr "Gaya hash NDK"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "LLVM passes different defaults to linkers on different platforms. After [this commit](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/95dcaef00379e893dabc61cf598fe51c9d03414e#diff-061e3e32cfa3dd06717856cc16465106a3b72520eb9b0c2954513f194bd1696f)  was merged into the NDK, `--hash-style=gnu` will be used on Debian by default. To change the hash style, `--hash-style=gnu` can be passed to the linker."
msgstr "LLVM meneruskan default yang berbeda ke linker pada platform yang berbeda. Setelah [commit ini](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/commit/95dcaef00379e893dabc61cf598fe51c9d03414e#diff-061e3e32cfa3dd06717856cc16465106a3b72520eb9b0c2954513f194bd1696f) digabungkan ke dalam NDK, `--hash-style=gnu` akan digunakan secara default di Debian. Untuk mengubah gaya hash, `--hash-style=gnu` dapat diteruskan ke linker."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "NDK clang version string in .comment section"
msgstr "String versi clang NDK di seksi .comment"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Since NDK r26, the Clang version string in the comment section is different when building on MacOS and Linux, which looks like"
msgstr "Sejak NDK r26, string versi Clang di seksi komentar berbeda saat dibangun di MacOS dan Linux, yang bentuknya seperti"

#. type: Fenced code block
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Android (12027248, +pgo, -bolt, +lto, +mlgo, based on r522817) clang version 18.0.1 (https://android.googlesource.com/toolchain/llvm-project d8003a456d14a3deb8054cdaa529ffbf02d9b262)\n"
msgstr "Android (12027248, +pgo, -bolt, +lto, +mlgo, based on r522817) clang version 18.0.1 (https://android.googlesource.com/toolchain/llvm-project d8003a456d14a3deb8054cdaa529ffbf02d9b262)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "due to different optimizations enabled for different platforms. The whole .comment section can be removed with"
msgstr "karena optimisasi yang berbeda diaktifkan untuk platform yang berbeda. Seluruh seksi .comment dapat dihapus dengan"

#. type: Fenced code block (console)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "objcopy --remove-section .comment <file>\n"
msgstr "objcopy --remove-section .comment <file>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "_platform_ Revisions"
msgstr "Revisi _platform_"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "In 2014, the Android SDK tools [were changed](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/37132313) to [stick two](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/ad2d07d%5E!/)  [data elements](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/5283fab%5E!/)  in `AndroidManifest.xml` as part of the build process: `platformBuildVersionName` and `platformBuildVersionCode`.  `platformBuildVersionName` includes the \"revision\" of the _platform_ package built against (e.g. `android-23`), however different \"revisions\" of the same _platform_ package cannot be installed in parallel.  Plus the SDK tools do not support specifying the required revision as part of the build process.  This often results in an otherwise reproducible build where the only difference is the `platformBuildVersionName` attribute."
msgstr "Pada tahun 2014, alat Android SDK [diubah](https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/37132313) untuk [menyisipkan dua](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/ad2d07d%5E!/) [elemen data](https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/5283fab%5E!/) ke dalam `AndroidManifest.xml` sebagai bagian dari proses build: `platformBuildVersionName` dan `platformBuildVersionCode`. `platformBuildVersionName` mencakup \"revision\" dari paket _platform_ yang dijadikan acuan build (misalnya `android-23`), namun \"revision\" yang berbeda dari paket _platform_ yang sama tidak dapat dipasang secara paralel. Selain itu, alat SDK tidak mendukung penentuan revision yang diperlukan sebagai bagian dari proses build. Hal ini sering menghasilkan build yang sebenarnya reproducible, tetapi satu-satunya perbedaan adalah atribut `platformBuildVersionName`."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "The _platform_ is part of the Android SDK that represents the standard library that is installed on the phone.  They have two parts to their version: \"version code\", which is an integer that represents the SDK release, and the \"revision\", which represents bugfix versions to each platform.  These versions can be seen in the included `build.prop` file.  Each revision has a different number in `ro.build.version.incremental`.  Gradle has no way to specify the revision in `compileSdkVersion` or `targetSdkVersion`.  Only one `platform-23` can be installed at a time, unlike `build-tools`, where every release can be installed in parallel."
msgstr "_Platform_ merupakan bagian dari Android SDK yang merepresentasikan standard library yang terpasang di ponsel. Platform memiliki dua bagian versi: \"version code\", yaitu integer yang merepresentasikan rilis SDK, dan \"revision\", yang merepresentasikan versi perbaikan bug untuk setiap platform. Versi-versi ini dapat dilihat di file `build.prop` yang disertakan. Setiap revision memiliki angka berbeda dalam `ro.build.version.incremental`. Gradle tidak memiliki cara untuk menentukan revision dalam `compileSdkVersion` atau `targetSdkVersion`. Hanya satu `platform-23` yang dapat dipasang pada satu waktu, tidak seperti `build-tools`, yang setiap rilisnya dapat dipasang secara paralel."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Here are two examples where all the differences are suspected to come from different revisions of the platform:"
msgstr "Berikut dua contoh ketika seluruh perbedaan diduga berasal dari revision platform yang berbeda:"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "<https://verification.f-droid.org/de.nico.ha_manager_25.apk.diffoscope.html>"
msgstr "<https://verification.f-droid.org/de.nico.ha_manager_25.apk.diffoscope.html>"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "<https://verification.f-droid.org/de.nico.asura_12.apk.diffoscope.html>"
msgstr "<https://verification.f-droid.org/de.nico.asura_12.apk.diffoscope.html>"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "PNG Crush/Crunch"
msgstr "PNG Crush/Crunch"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "A standard part of the Android build process is to run some kind of PNG optimization tool, like `aapt singleCrunch`, `pngcrush`, `zopflipng` or `optipng`.  These do not provide deterministic output, it is still an open question as to why.  Since PNGs are normally committed to the source repo, a workaround to this problem is to run the tool of your choice on the PNG files, then commit those changes to the source repo (e.g. `git`).  Then, disable the default PNG optimization process by adding this to `build.gradle`:"
msgstr "Sebagai bagian standar dari proses build Android, jalankan semacam alat optimasi PNG, seperti `aapt singleCrunch`, `pngcrush`, `zopflipng`, atau `optipng`. Alat-alat ini tidak menghasilkan output yang deterministik; masih menjadi pertanyaan terbuka mengapa demikian. Karena PNG biasanya sudah dikomit ke source repo, workaround untuk masalah ini adalah menjalankan alat pilihan Anda pada file PNG, lalu mengomit perubahan tersebut ke source repo (misalnya `git`). Setelah itu, nonaktifkan proses optimasi PNG bawaan dengan menambahkan ini ke `build.gradle`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"android {\n"
"    aaptOptions {\n"
"        cruncherEnabled = false\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"android {\n"
"    aaptOptions {\n"
"        cruncherEnabled = false\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Note that tools such as `svgo` can do similar optimization to SVG files."
msgstr "Perlu dicatat bahwa alat seperti `svgo` dapat melakukan optimasi serupa pada file SVG."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "PNGs generated from vector drawables"
msgstr "PNG yang dihasilkan dari vector drawable"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "[Android Gradle plugin generates PNG resources from vector drawables for old Android versions](https://developer.android.com/reference/tools/gradle-api/7.3/com/android/build/api/dsl/VectorDrawables#generateddensities).  Unfortunately, the generated PNG files are not reproducible."
msgstr "[Android Gradle plugin menghasilkan resource PNG dari vector drawable untuk versi Android lama](https://developer.android.com/reference/tools/gradle-api/7.3/com/android/build/api/dsl/VectorDrawables#generateddensities). Sayangnya, file PNG yang dihasilkan tidak reproducible."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "You can disable generating the PNGs by adding this to `build.gradle`:"
msgstr "Anda dapat menonaktifkan pembuatan PNG dengan menambahkan potongan berikut ke `build.gradle`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"android {\n"
"    defaultConfig {\n"
"        vectorDrawables.generatedDensities = []\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"android {\n"
"    defaultConfig {\n"
"        vectorDrawables.generatedDensities = []\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "R8 Optimizer"
msgstr "R8 Optimizer"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "It appears that some R8 optimizations are non-deterministic, producing different bytecode on different build runs."
msgstr "Tampaknya beberapa optimisasi R8 bersifat non-deterministik, menghasilkan bytecode yang berbeda pada run build yang berbeda."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "For instance, R8 tries to optimize `ServiceLoader` usage making a static list of all services in the code.  The order of this list may be different (or even incomplete) on each build run.  The only way to avoid this behaviour is disabling such optimizations declaring optimized classes in `proguard-rules.pro`:"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, R8 mencoba mengoptimalkan penggunaan `ServiceLoader` dengan membuat daftar statis semua service dalam kode. Urutan daftar ini dapat berbeda (atau bahkan tidak lengkap) pada setiap build run. Satu-satunya cara untuk menghindari perilaku ini adalah menonaktifkan optimisasi tersebut dengan mendeklarasikan class yang dioptimalkan di `proguard-rules.pro`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (proguard)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"-keep class kotlinx.coroutines.CoroutineExceptionHandler\n"
"-keep class kotlinx.coroutines.internal.MainDispatcherFactory\n"
msgstr ""
"-keep class kotlinx.coroutines.CoroutineExceptionHandler\n"
"-keep class kotlinx.coroutines.internal.MainDispatcherFactory\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Be careful with R8.  Always test your builds multiple times and disable optimizations which produce non-deterministic output."
msgstr "Berhati-hatilah dengan R8. Selalu uji build Anda beberapa kali dan nonaktifkan optimisasi yang menghasilkan output non-deterministik."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "If the DEX bytecode is different and depends on the number of CPU cores, try to update R8 to version 8.6.33, 8.7.20, 8.8 or newer as some issues were fixed in this regard."
msgstr "Jika bytecode DEX berbeda dan bergantung pada jumlah core CPU, coba perbarui R8 ke versi 8.6.33, 8.7.20, 8.8, atau yang lebih baru karena beberapa masalah telah diperbaiki dalam hal ini."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEX classes in wrong order"
msgstr "Kelas DEX dalam urutan yang salah"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Even if the contents might match, if the classes file names are switched, reproducibility will fail. This was fixed for bundles in AGP 8.8 but we've seen this issue for APKs too. Try with the newer AGP first."
msgstr "Bahkan jika isinya mungkin cocok, jika nama file kelas tertukar, reproducibility akan gagal. Hal ini sudah diperbaiki untuk bundle di AGP 8.8, tetapi kami juga melihat masalah ini pada APK. Cobalah versi AGP yang lebih baru terlebih dahulu."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Resource Shrinker"
msgstr "Resource Shrinker"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "It's possible to reduce the APK file size by removing unused resources from the package.  This is useful when a project depends on some bloated libraries such as AppCompat, especially when R8/ProGuard code shrinking is used."
msgstr "Ukuran file APK dapat dikurangi dengan menghapus resource yang tidak digunakan dari package. Ini berguna ketika sebuah project bergantung pada library yang besar seperti AppCompat, terutama ketika code shrinking R8/ProGuard digunakan."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "However, it might be possible that resource shrinker will increase the APK size on different platforms, especially if there are not many resources to shrink, in which case the original APK will be used instead of the shrunk one (non-deterministic behaviour of Gradle plugin).  Avoid using resource shrinker unless it decreases the APK file size significantly."
msgstr "Namun, bisa jadi resource shrinker justru akan menambah ukuran APK di platform yang berbeda, terutama jika tidak banyak resource untuk diperkecil, dalam hal ini APK asli akan digunakan sebagai gantinya untuk yang diperkecil (perilaku Gradle plugin yang tidak deterministik). Hindari menggunakan resource shrinker kecuali jika ukurannya benar-benar berkurang secara signifikan."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "VCS Info"
msgstr "Informasi VCS"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Since Android Gradle Plugin 8.3, VCS info is generated by default and bundled in the apk in `META-INF/version-control-info.textproto`, e.g."
msgstr "Sejak Android Gradle Plugin 8.3, informasi VCS dibuat secara default dan dibundel di dalam apk pada `META-INF/version-control-info.textproto`, misalnya"

#. type: Fenced code block (Proto)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"repositories {\n"
"  system: GIT\n"
"  local_root_path: \"$PROJECT_DIR\"\n"
"  revision: \"3a443877cd53e37d85cbc52adc8cfd558919d373\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"repositories {\n"
"  system: GIT\n"
"  local_root_path: \"$PROJECT_DIR\"\n"
"  revision: \"3a443877cd53e37d85cbc52adc8cfd558919d373\"\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "While we understand that developers build and test during their normal workflow, please upload release APKs built after tagging, from a clean tree at the actual tagged commit (i.e. without local changes or remaining artefacts from previous builds). Only in exceptional cases, when you cannot do this, should `vcsInfo` be disabled (as this might otherwise cause problems), which can be done as follows:"
msgstr "Walaupun kami memahami bahwa developer membangun dan menguji selama alur kerja normal mereka, harap unggah APK rilis yang dibangun setelah tagging, dari tree yang bersih pada commit tag yang sebenarnya (yaitu tanpa perubahan lokal atau artefak yang tersisa dari build sebelumnya). Hanya dalam kasus luar biasa, ketika Anda tidak dapat melakukannya, `vcsInfo` boleh dinonaktifkan (karena jika tidak, ini mungkin menimbulkan masalah), yang dapat dilakukan sebagai berikut:"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    buildTypes {\n"
"        release {\n"
"           vcsInfo.include false\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZIP metadata"
msgstr "metadata ZIP"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "APKs use the ZIP file format, which was originally designed around the MSDOS FAT filesystem.  UNIX file permissions were added as an extension.  APKs only need the most basic ZIP format, without any of the extensions.  These extensions are often stripped out in the final release signing process.  But the APK build process can add them.  For example:"
msgstr "APK menggunakan format file ZIP, yang awalnya dirancang untuk filesystem MSDOS FAT. Izin file UNIX ditambahkan sebagai ekstensi. APK hanya memerlukan format ZIP paling dasar, tanpa ekstensi tambahan. Ekstensi ini sering dihapus dalam proses penandatanganan rilis akhir. Namun proses build APK dapat menambahkannya. Misalnya:"

#. type: Fenced code block (diff)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"--- a2dp.Vol_137.apk\n"
"+++ sigcp_a2dp.Vol_137.apk\n"
"@@ -1,50 +1,50 @@\n"
"--rw----     2.0 fat     8976 bX defN 79-Nov-30 00:00 AndroidManifest.xml\n"
"--rw----     2.0 fat  1958312 bX defN 79-Nov-30 00:00 classes.dex\n"
"--rw----     1.0 fat    78984 bx stor 79-Nov-30 00:00 resources.arsc\n"
"+-rw-rw-rw-  2.3 unx     8976 b- defN 80-000-00 00:00 AndroidManifest.xml\n"
"+-rw----     2.4 fat  1958312 b- defN 80-000-00 00:00 classes.dex\n"
"+-rw-rw-rw-  2.3 unx    78984 b- stor 80-000-00 00:00 resources.arsc\n"
msgstr ""
"--- a2dp.Vol_137.apk\n"
"+++ sigcp_a2dp.Vol_137.apk\n"
"@@ -1,50 +1,50 @@\n"
"--rw----     2.0 fat     8976 bX defN 79-Nov-30 00:00 AndroidManifest.xml\n"
"--rw----     2.0 fat  1958312 bX defN 79-Nov-30 00:00 classes.dex\n"
"--rw----     1.0 fat    78984 bx stor 79-Nov-30 00:00 resources.arsc\n"
"+-rw-rw-rw-  2.3 unx     8976 b- defN 80-000-00 00:00 AndroidManifest.xml\n"
"+-rw----     2.4 fat  1958312 b- defN 80-000-00 00:00 classes.dex\n"
"+-rw-rw-rw-  2.3 unx    78984 b- stor 80-000-00 00:00 resources.arsc\n"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mismatched Toolchains"
msgstr "Mismatched Toolchains"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Different toolchains may produce different binaries. A usual case is when more than one JDK version/distribution are used to build the APK. Sometimes even Gradle may mix versions of JDKs to build an APK. To avoid such problems unused JDKs should be removed."
msgstr "Toolchain yang berbeda dapat menghasilkan binary yang berbeda. Kasus yang umum adalah ketika lebih dari satu versi/distribusi JDK digunakan untuk membangun APK. Terkadang bahkan Gradle dapat mencampur versi JDK untuk membangun APK. Untuk menghindari masalah seperti itu, JDK yang tidak digunakan sebaiknya dihapus."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "The APK diff will have entries in the `classes.dex` files like this, e.g. Java 17 vs Java 11:"
msgstr "Perbedaan file `classes.dex` akibat versi Java yang berbeda dapat terlihat seperti:"

#. type: Bullet: '-    '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid ".annotation system Ldalvik/annotation/Signature;"
msgstr ".annotation system Ldalvik/annotation/Signature;"

#. type: Bullet: '-        '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "value = {"
msgstr "value = {"

#. type: Bullet: '-            '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "\"()V\""
msgstr "\"()V\""

#. type: Bullet: '-        '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "}"
msgstr "}"

#. type: Bullet: '-    '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid ".end annotation"
msgstr ".end annotation"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Or like this, e.g. Java 17 vs Java 21:"
msgstr "atau seperti ini, misalnya antara build menggunakan Java 17 dan Java 21:"

#. type: Bullet: '-    '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid ".annotation system Ldalvik/annotation/MethodParameters;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '-        '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "accessFlags = {"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '-            '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "0x8010"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '-        '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "names = {"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '-            '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "null"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Different NDK versions also produce different binaries. Generally this can be recognized via the metadata, e.g. LLD version, in the native libs. However, since NDK r26d a weird behaviour is observed that sometimes only the `.shstrtab` sections in ELF of the native libs are changed when NDK is installed. The native libs may be built along with the app or fetched from maven repo. If AGP finds that the NDK is installed, it will use NDK to strip the native lib but in fact it only messes up the `.shstrtab` section of the native lib. The NDK setup needs to be checked carefully to ensure it matches upstream setup, including the NDK version and if it's used by AGP."
msgstr "Versi NDK yang berbeda juga menghasilkan binary yang berbeda. Secara umum, hal ini dapat dikenali melalui metadata, misalnya versi LLD, di native libs. Namun, sejak NDK r26d diamati perilaku aneh bahwa terkadang hanya bagian `.shstrtab` dalam ELF dari native libs yang berubah ketika NDK dipasang. Native libs tersebut dapat dibangun bersama aplikasi atau diambil dari maven repo. Jika AGP mendeteksi bahwa NDK terpasang, ia akan menggunakan NDK untuk melakukan strip pada native lib, tetapi sebenarnya hal itu hanya mengacaukan bagian `.shstrtab` dari native lib. Setup NDK perlu diperiksa dengan cermat untuk memastikan bahwa ia cocok dengan setup upstream, termasuk versi NDK dan apakah NDK digunakan oleh AGP."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "F-Droid build server currently supports the following JDK versions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "25 from Debian Trixie"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "21 from Debian Trixie"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "17 from Debian Bookworm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "11 from Debian Bullseye"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "8 from Debian Sid"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Note that versions not from the current Debian stable (Trixie) might become unavailable as time passes, so you are encouraged to update as much as possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support 16 KB page sizes"
msgstr "Dukungan untuk ukuran halaman 16 KB"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Beginning with Android 15, Android supports devices that are configured to use a page size of 16 KB (16 KB devices). If your app uses any NDK libraries, either directly or indirectly through an SDK, then you will need to rebuild your app for it to work on these 16 KB devices. More info [here](https://developer.android.com/guide/practices/page-sizes)"
msgstr "Mulai Android 15, Android mendukung perangkat yang dikonfigurasi menggunakan page size 16 KB (perangkat 16 KB). Jika aplikasi Anda menggunakan library NDK, baik secara langsung maupun tidak langsung melalui SDK, maka Anda harus membangun ulang aplikasi agar dapat bekerja pada perangkat 16 KB ini. Informasi lebih lanjut [di sini](https://developer.android.com/guide/practices/page-sizes)"

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Language-specific instructions"
msgstr "Instruksi khusus bahasa"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Native libraries may be built with various tools and languages. Though they suffer from similar reproducible build issues, the methods for fixing them are different. Some known solutions are listed below:"
msgstr "Native libraries dapat dibangun dengan berbagai tool dan bahasa. Walaupun mereka mengalami masalah reproducible build yang serupa, metode untuk memperbaikinya berbeda. Beberapa solusi yang diketahui tercantum di bawah ini:"

#. type: Title #####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "ndk-build"
msgstr "ndk-build"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`LOCAL_CFLAGS += <compiler args>` and `LOCAL_LDFLAGS += -Wl,<linker args>` can be added to `Android.mk` files or to\n"
"`build.gradle`/`build.gradle.kts`:\n"
msgstr "Anda dapat menambahkan `LOCAL_CFLAGS += mpiler args>` dan `LOCAL_LDFLAGS += -Wl,<linker args>` ke dalam berkas `Android.mk` atau ke dalam `build.gradle`/`build.gradle.kts`:\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"android {\n"
"    defaultConfig {\n"
"        externalNativeBuild {\n"
"            ndkBuild {\n"
"                arguments \"LOCAL_CFLAGS+=<compiler args> LOCAL_LDFLAGS+=-Wl,<linker args>\"\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"android {\n"
"    defaultConfig {\n"
"        externalNativeBuild {\n"
"            ndkBuild {\n"
"                arguments \"LOCAL_CFLAGS+=<compiler args> LOCAL_LDFLAGS+=-Wl,<linker args>\"\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Title #####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "CMake"
msgstr "CMake"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For CMake versions since 3.13, `add_compile_options(\"<compiler args>\")` and `add_link_options(LINKER:<linker args>)` can\n"
"be added to `CMakeLists.txt` globally, e.g. to remove `build-id`:\n"
msgstr "Untuk versi CMake sejak 3.13, `add_compile_options(\"<compiler args>\")` dan `add_link_options(LINKER:<linker args>)` dapat ditambahkan ke `CMakeLists.txt` secara global, misalnya untuk menghapus `build-id`:\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (cmake)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "add_link_options(\"LINKER:--build-id=none\")\n"
msgstr "add_link_options(\"LINKER:--build-id=none\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This command only works for libraries added after this command is invoked, so it should\n"
"be invoked at the beginning of the CMake file. For CMake versions before 3.13,\n"
"`target_compile_options(<target> PRIVATE <compiler args>)` and `target_link_libraries(<target> LINKER:<linker args>)` can be used instead for\n"
"every target. It can also be set in Gradle files:\n"
msgstr ""
"Perintah ini hanya berlaku untuk pustaka yang ditambahkan setelah perintah ini dipanggil, jadi sebaiknya diletakkan di awal berkas CMake.\n"
"Untuk versi CMake sebelum 3.13, gunakan `target_compile_options(<target> PRIVATE mpiler args>)` dan `target_link_libraries(<target> LINKER:<linker args>)` untuk setiap target.\n"
"Alternatifnya, konfigurasi ini juga dapat ditetapkan langsung di berkas Gradle:\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"android {\n"
"    defaultConfig {\n"
"        externalNativeBuild.cmake {\n"
"          cFlags \"<compiler args> -Wl,<linker args>\" // or\n"
"          arguments \"-DCMAKE_C_FLAGS=<compiler args> -DCMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS=-Wl,<linker args>\"\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"android {\n"
"    defaultConfig {\n"
"        externalNativeBuild.cmake {\n"
"          cFlags \"<compiler args> -Wl,<linker args>\" // or\n"
"          arguments \"-DCMAKE_C_FLAGS=<compiler args> -DCMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS=-Wl,<linker args>\"\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "And this can also be used to change the behavior of libs from pub for Flutter apps, e.g. for `jni` pub:"
msgstr "Dan ini juga dapat digunakan untuk mengubah perilaku library dari pub untuk aplikasi Flutter, misalnya untuk `jni` pub:"

#. type: Fenced code block (kotlin)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"import com.android.build.gradle.LibraryExtension\n"
"subprojects {\n"
"    plugins.withId(\"com.android.library\") {\n"
"        if (name == \"jni\") {\n"
"            extensions.configure<LibraryExtension>(\"android\") {\n"
"                defaultConfig {\n"
"                    externalNativeBuild {\n"
"                        cmake {\n"
"                            arguments += \"-DCMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS=-Wl,--build-id=none\"\n"
"                        }\n"
"                    }\n"
"                }\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"import com.android.build.gradle.LibraryExtension\n"
"subprojects {\n"
"    plugins.withId(\"com.android.library\") {\n"
"        if (name == \"jni\") {\n"
"            extensions.configure<LibraryExtension>(\"android\") {\n"
"                defaultConfig {\n"
"                    externalNativeBuild {\n"
"                        cmake {\n"
"                            arguments += \"-DCMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS=-Wl,--build-id=none\"\n"
"                        }\n"
"                    }\n"
"                }\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "The `-ffile-prefix-map` flag can be used to remove embedded build path. It can be added to `CMakeLists.txt` directly:"
msgstr "Flag `-ffile-prefix-map` dapat digunakan untuk menghapus embedded build path. Flag ini dapat ditambahkan langsung ke `CMakeLists.txt`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (cmake)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "add_compile_options(\"-ffile-prefix-map=${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}=.\")\n"
msgstr "add_compile_options(\"-ffile-prefix-map=${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}=.\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "or in `build.gradle`:"
msgstr "atau di `build.gradle`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"externalNativeBuild {\n"
"    cmake {\n"
"        cFlags \"-ffile-prefix-map=${rootDir}=.\"\n"
"        cppFlags \"-ffile-prefix-map=${rootDir}=.\"\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"externalNativeBuild {\n"
"    cmake {\n"
"        cFlags \"-ffile-prefix-map=${rootDir}=.\"\n"
"        cppFlags \"-ffile-prefix-map=${rootDir}=.\"\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Title #####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Golang"
msgstr "Golang"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Linker arguments can be added to `CGO_LDFLAGS`. Some other useful arguments that can be passed to `go build` are `-ldflags=\"-buildid=\"`, `-trimpath` (to avoid embedded build paths) and `-buildvcs=false`."
msgstr "Argumen linker dapat ditambahkan ke `CGO_LDFLAGS`. Beberapa argumen lain yang berguna yang dapat diteruskan ke `go build` adalah `-ldflags=\"-buildid=\"`, `-trimpath` (untuk menghindari embedded build paths), dan `-buildvcs=false`."

#. type: Title #####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rust"
msgstr "Rust"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compiler and linker arguments can be added to [Cargo `build.rustflags`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config.html#buildrustflags) and [rustc Codegen Options](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/codegen-options/index.html).\n"
"Linker arguments can be added with `-C link-args=-Wl,<linker args>` and `--remap-path-prefix=<old>=<new>`\n"
"can be added to strip build paths.\n"
msgstr ""
"Argumen compiler dan linker dapat ditambahkan ke [Cargo `build.rustflags`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config.html#buildrustflags) dan [rustc Codegen Options](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/codegen-options/index.html).\n"
"Argumen linker dapat ditambahkan dengan `-C link-args=-Wl,<linker args>` dan `--remap-path-prefix=<old>=<new>` dapat ditambahkan untuk menghapus build path.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "An unstable feature [trim-paths](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/unstable.html#profile-trim-paths-option) is added to Cargo to remove all the absolute paths in rust."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Rust toolchain should be pinned to the same version as upstream. This can be done when installing rustup with `rustup-init.sh -y --default-toolchain <version>`.\n"
msgstr "Rust toolchain sebaiknya dipin ke versi yang sama seperti upstream. Ini dapat dilakukan saat memasang rustup dengan `rustup-init.sh -y --default-toolchain <version>`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "When `openssl` crate uses vendored OpenSSL build, the OpenSSL lib needs to be configured specially to be reproducible. `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` can be set to remove the embedded timestamps and `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` can be set to a absolute path, e.g. `/tmp/build` to make the embedded path reproducible between different machines. NDK also need to be in the same path which can be solved by linking it to the same path."
msgstr "Saat crate `openssl` menggunakan build OpenSSL vendored, library OpenSSL perlu dikonfigurasi secara khusus agar reproducible. `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` dapat diatur untuk menghapus embedded timestamps dan `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` dapat diatur ke path absolut, misalnya `/tmp/build`, agar embedded path menjadi reproducible di antara mesin yang berbeda. NDK juga perlu berada pada path yang sama, yang dapat diatasi dengan menautkannya ke path yang sama."

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "`CARGO_HOME` path plays an important part too and ends up in the built libs, it's recommended to match it between builds, e.g. export it before running `rustup`, or any other build commands, and don't forget to source `env` from it."
msgstr "Path `CARGO_HOME` juga memainkan peran penting dan berakhir di built libs; disarankan untuk menyamakannya antara build, misalnya export sebelum menjalankan `rustup`, atau perintah build lainnya, dan jangan lupa untuk men-source `env` darinya."

#. type: Title ####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Library-specific instructions"
msgstr "Instruksi khusus library"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "Some libraries generate non-deterministic code due to timestamps, unsorted iterations etc. Some known fixes are documented below:"
msgstr "Beberapa library menghasilkan code yang non-deterministik karena timestamps, iterasi yang tidak diurutkan, dan sebagainya. Beberapa perbaikan yang diketahui didokumentasikan di bawah ini:"

#. type: Title #####
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "AboutLibraries Gradle plugin"
msgstr "Plugin AboutLibraries Gradle"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "You can prevent this plugin (`com.mikepenz.aboutlibraries.plugin`) from adding a timestamp to the JSON file it generates by adding this to `build.gradle`:"
msgstr "Anda dapat mencegah plugin ini (`com.mikepenz.aboutlibraries.plugin`) menambahkan timestamp ke file JSON yang dihasilkannya dengan menambahkan ini ke `build.gradle`:"

#. type: Fenced code block (groovy)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"aboutLibraries {\n"
"    // Remove the \"generated\" timestamp to allow for reproducible builds\n"
"    excludeFields = [\"generated\"]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"aboutLibraries {\n"
"    // Remove the \"generated\" timestamp to allow for reproducible builds\n"
"    excludeFields = [\"generated\"]\n"
"}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
msgid "For `build.gradle.kts`, add this instead:"
msgstr "Untuk `build.gradle.kts`, tambahkan ini sebagai gantinya:"

#. type: Fenced code block (kotlin)
#: _docs/Reproducible_Builds.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"aboutLibraries {\n"
"    // Remove the \"generated\" timestamp to allow for reproducible builds\n"
"    excludeFields = arrayOf(\"generated\")\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""
"aboutLibraries {\n"
"    // Remove the \"generated\" timestamp to allow for reproducible builds\n"
"    excludeFields = arrayOf(\"generated\")\n"
"}\n"

